# NOTE on the knowledge build products. `scripts/build-knowledge.mjs` WRITES
# `resources/knowledge/stellaris/**` (TOML, derived from the hand-written `knowledge/*.md`) and
# `src/generated/knowledge.mjs` (the snapshot the server embeds). They are TRACKED, not ignored:
# this project has no build step, `npx rstellarisgui` / `node src/index.mjs` runs the sources
# directly, and `package.json` ships `src` and `resources`. An ignored `src/generated/knowledge.mjs`
# would make a fresh clone a server with NO KNOWLEDGE BASE until someone ran the build - and a clone
# that does not work is worse than a generated file in the repository. `node scripts/build-knowledge.mjs`
# regenerates both deterministically, and `scripts/selftest.mjs` fails if either is stale.
# The sibling RStellarisScribe cites this same reasoning in its own .gitignore; the two must agree.

